{# A smith's or tailor's deferred commissions: JobBlacksmithFaction and JobTailorFaction by decimal FormID 330013 / 525992
   (Skyrim.esm 0x0005091D / 0x000806A8; an EditorID needs po3, an optional plugin, and Inja reads no hex literal); one in both
   reads as a smith. crafting_commission is the open orders, one "- " line each ("" with none). The how-to and the order rules
   render only in NPC dialogue (responseTarget type player, npc or all). #}
{% set _commission_smith = get_faction_rank(npc.UUID, 330013) >= 0 %}
{% if _commission_smith or get_faction_rank(npc.UUID, 525992) >= 0 %}
{% set _commission_info = crafting_commission(npc.UUID) %}
{% set _commission_howto = render_mode == "full" and default(responseTarget.type, "none") != "none" %}
{% if _commission_howto or _commission_info != "" %}
{% if _commission_smith %}
## Your Forge — Commissions
{% else %}
## Your Shop — Commissions
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if _commission_howto %}
{% if _commission_smith %}
As a smith you can take **deferred commissions**: forge work the customer collects later, at a price you set. These actions are in the **Crafting** action category:
{% else %}
As a tailor you can take **deferred commissions**: clothes made to order that the customer collects later, at a price you set. These actions are in the **Crafting** action category:
{% endif %}
- **CommissionItem**: accept an order to be collected later. Name a ready time in your own words; the customer pays half the price now and half on pickup.{% if _commission_smith %} Use **CraftItem** only for work you finish on the spot.{% endif %} For an item that also goes by another name, written "Name (Game Name)", pass the whole name as written.
- **CollectCommission**: when the customer comes back for a finished piece, this one action shows the balance, takes the gold and hands the item over. No Items or Economy action is needed for a commission.
{% if _commission_smith %}
- **Pricing is yours.** Price by metal and effort (a rough guide, not a rule): a steel weapon a few dozen septims, dwarven or elven work a couple of hundred, glass or ebony a few hundred to a thousand, daedric or dragon work well over a thousand; armor and multiples cost more. Say the total as a plain number, and pass that same number as quotedTotal on CommissionItem.
{% else %}
- **Pricing is yours.** Price by cloth and craft (a rough guide, not a rule): plain clothes or boots a handful of septims to a few dozen, fine clothes around a hundred, a noble's finery a few hundred; multiples cost more. Say the total as a plain number, and pass that same number as quotedTotal on CommissionItem.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if _commission_info != "" %}
Orders on your books:
{{ _commission_info }}
{% if _commission_howto %}
- When a piece is finished and ready to collect and its customer is here for it, greet them in a line, then select the **Crafting** action category, then **CollectCommission**. Do NOT narrate the handover instead: words alone move no item and no gold.
- If an order is still being worked on, tell them to come back later and hand nothing over.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
